  "scope": "The actual 208-slot original-row width traversal calls the real fraction-width machine for each original record, saves its returned size word, recursively measures the literal original tail, and calls the actual maximum on both returned roots. It returns exactly BinaryFractionalGuesses.widthList and inputWidth for the original typed row. Both words and original row/source remain on the same physical heap. The terminal-inclusive bound uses only the sum of original padded numerator/denominator bits and original row length; no width result or width certificate is supplied. Twelve actual cases cover empty, padded, duplicate, increasing, larger-head and larger-tail rows. Actual grid/lambda/guess construction and full original solver composition remain separate.",
  "pending": [
    "independent semantic review",
    "combined production integration and exact CI"
  ]
